    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Given a drawing of a single closed shape, count its concave corners.<br><br>The outline is made of <const>/</const> and <const>\\</const>; every other character is a space.<br>It never crosses or touches itself.<br><br>A corner is concave when it points toward the inside of the shape.<br><br>A shape is convex exactly when the answer is <const>0</const>.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> an integer <var>N</var>, the width and height of the drawing.<br><strong>Next <var>N</var> lines:</strong> a string <var>LINE</var> of exactly <var>N</var> characters, spaces included.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> an integer, the number of concave corners of the shape.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">2 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 31</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">8\n        \n /\\  /\\ \n/  \\/  \\\n\\      /\n \\    / \n  \\  /  \n   \\/   \n        </pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
